description:
Line 986: `let coap = &packet[48..];` is executed unconditionally in the UDP branch (nh==17), but the only length guard is at line 976 which only protects the MQTT-SN block. If packet.len() is 40-47 bytes with next_header=17 (UDP), the slice panics.

Attack vector: Send a malformed IPv6+UDP packet with only partial UDP header (e.g., 42 bytes). The compressor panics, crashing the node.

Trigger: Any packet where packet[6]==17 (UDP) && 40 <= packet.len() < 48

Fix: Guard the slice creation:
```rust
let is_oscore = if packet.len() >= 52 {
    has_oscore_option(&packet[48..])
} else {
    false
};
```
